WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Batman, the video game.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:09.400
He's totally new, totally tough, and he'll stop at nothing to make sure justice prevails.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:32.580
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.580
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.860
And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.820
And that back of the box was totally, totally off, right?

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.520
Oh, sorry, can you say it again?

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.280
Yeah, it was, he's totally new, totally tough.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:54.460
Like, nobody, Batman, maybe in the 60s for the Adam West version, but like, this is loosely

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:59.800
based off of the 1989 film, and I just feel like that doesn't make any sense, right?

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:08.800
I mean, you know, it's only a year old, this is how most people were introduced to Batman.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.240
Not really. I don't know.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.460
You're right, it's off.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.060
Yeah, it's totally new, just in reference to, like, yeah, because it's the new movie.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.900
Yes, that's what I would be thinking of.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.020
Or is it like, hey, we came up with a new idea, Batman.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:28.280
No, I think it's the movie, but even then, like, the movie is really, it's not, it's not

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.360
like they reinvented Batman in this movie.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:35.500
Now, I understand that the movie did wonders for Batman, like, as a brand, and like, you

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.580
know, reignited a lot of, you know, interest in the general population.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:45.320
Of course, comic people were already having their Batman renaissance with Batman Year

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:51.120
One and The Dark Knight Returns, being two comics that were released the two previous

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.420
years from the release of this film.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:02:00.740
But, nevertheless, I don't think that the Tim Burton world of Batman ever would have used

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.800
the word totally, you know?

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:08.740
Yeah, maybe not. I don't think that that would have flown there, and I don't think, even in this loosely based

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:13.180
NES game, and I'm going to keep mentioning that it's loosely based, because, obviously,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.200
Batman, the video game, is using imagery from the movie, but that's kind of where the similarities

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.820
stop. Like, yeah, you have the Joker at the end of the game, but otherwise, like, this is not

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.720
yourself, like, being Batman working through the plot of the movie.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.620
It's just a Batman video game that happened to come out after the release of the movie,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.200
so they said, yeah, we could do this, we could tie them together.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.060
They didn't call it Batman the movie the game, which is a step up, they just called it Batman

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.700
the video game, but it's definitely not the movie.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:50.240
Yeah, I mean, the fact that one of the first things that you might do when playing this game

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:58.120
is go through your sort of utility belt and find a gun, you know that it's not entirely,

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.880
like, Batman researched.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:07.100
Is it like a gun gun, or does it shoot some weird, like, rocket propelled, like, gadget

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.720
or something? It says it shoots a spear, which sounds worse than a gun.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:21.020
Yeah. It says it's Batman's spear gun, which, again, is funny, but to shoot a short pointed spear

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.440
at the enemies, so not sure how Stark Bullets it is.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.880
As long as it's not a totally not K in Batman's book.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.000
Yeah, they're all dull tips.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.540
They forgot to mention that part.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.900
It's Nerf. Right.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.580
And, yes, he does have his Batarang as well, and then he has the Dirk, but I just consider

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.680
that a, like, what are those things?

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:43.060
Ninja Stars, you know, like, the Dirk.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.880
I don't know if that's an actual reference.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.100
You mean, like, the big gun, where it turns into three bullets?

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.820
Is that what that is?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.480
I guess it is.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.720
Yeah, yeah, I guess you're right. Yeah, it's the one that shoots in three different directions.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.980
I was thinking of the symbol.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.980
The symbol looked like a Ninja Star.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.080
Got it, got it.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.460
Yeah, okay. I like that triple one.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.960
I use that quite often, but I had a question.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.220
I don't know what it was. Oh, you know what?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.720
Speaking of the Batarang, though, that thing.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.320
Now, this is just a, don't even take this as a complaint.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:20.620
It's just a funny little thing I noticed, where the whole point of this boomerang coming

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.500
back to you is it comes back to you, right?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:23.880
Why do you have ammo for that?

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.100
I keep running out of ammo for my boomerang.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.240
It's all the times he didn't catch it.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.180
It looks like he caught it, but he didn't.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.140
I'm watching him catch it.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.520
No, no, no. It just looks like it.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.000
Yeah, no, you guys all bring up great points.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.400
We're not going to talk about the movie, I suppose, unless anybody feels strongly about

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.060
the Tim Burton Batman movie.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.300
It was fine.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.480
Fine. Interesting.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.500
I don't really remember much of it.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.440
Some people still think it's one of the best.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.760
I mean, it's a good movie.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.760
Yeah. I wouldn't say it's up there, though.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.200
I think it's a good movie. I don't think it's up there.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.720
Yeah, I don't think...

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:01.000
I prefer the Nolan movies, but I don't have any...

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.460
I like the aesthetic of the old ones, you know?

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.460
Or at least this one.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:06.780
The other ones were terrible.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.380
No, no, no. The next one, Batman Returns, with Danny DeVito as the penguin.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.760
That one, aesthetically, took everything up another notch.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.960
Yeah, that...

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.340
I guess I meant more so the Jerry Bruckheimer ones.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.720
Got it, yeah, yeah. Clooney and Kilmer.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.060
Yeah, with the nipples.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.360
You know. Is this... Oh, yeah.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.620
But this is, like, officially licensed, though, right?

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.640
Of, like, of that movie.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.640
Yes. Not just Batman the character.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.260
Yeah, he says lines in the movie at some point, right?

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.600
Like, clearly Jack Nicholson?

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:39.600
Maybe not clearly Jack Nicholson.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.140
Maybe I didn't see as many cutscenes as you, but...

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:49.140
I'd say that, like, it's at least saying lines from the movie, so it's 100% based on the movie.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:57.220
Yeah, it's clearly Jack Nicholson as much as the main menu screen when you first see Batman is clearly Michael Keaton.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.280
Like, it's pixelated, so it's like, ah, you could make the argument.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.140
Like, I doubt they paid Michael Keaton in any shape or form for this.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:09.660
But, you know, it looks close enough, and that's definitely the same exact costume he wore in the movie.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:15.320
Well, the image that I'm talking about, I mean, I was not really thinking about the movie.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:20.420
I'd forgotten that Jack Nicholson was in the movie, and I saw his sprite, and I was like, oh, that's a sprite of Jack Nicholson.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.320
Like, I immediately jumped out at me.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:23.820
Got it, got it.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:24.720
That is funny.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.100
I do know which one you're talking about because it's also in the manual.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.120
You're talking about when you're, like, he's on those TVs?

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.440
Oh, yeah. I don't remember.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:33.860
I'm scrubbing through right now here.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:38.700
It's in, like, when you get, it's the stage four when you get to the laboratory.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.980
Yes, yeah. Yeah.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.660
So you thought, like, wow, Batman went to that hotel in Colorado?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:53.260
Yeah, yeah. I mean, I knew that Jack Nicholson was in the movie, but I just, like, had forgotten, and it just shocked me for a second to see.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.180
What is that, the Overlook Hotel?

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.000
The Overlook Hotel, yeah.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.900
Yeah, okay. All right.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.800
So, Hotel in Colorado or the Overlook Hotel, you know, they're both famous.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:09.320
Yeah. Anyway, to get back on track, in this side-scrolling action game, you play as Batman through five levels, loosely based.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:16.000
And again, they're words, not mine, but loosely based on the 1989 film before a final showdown with the Joker.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:23.380
And I know it's kind of a meme to say that, you know, the Arkham games really make you feel like Batman.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:33.980
So, since I can't resist saying it as well, if the test of a Batman video game is whether you feel like Batman or not, does this game make you feel like Batman?

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:40.460
If not Batman, it makes me feel like Batman.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.360
I'm a mutant video game character.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:59.000
Because I'd say when it comes to these side-scrollers, a lot of them just sort of either try and emulate Mario, or they do something completely different, or they do something completely failure-tastic.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:08.140
Whereas I think this one actually has its own feel and style to it, where things feel fluid, but not like Mario.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:19.760
And the parts that don't really feel fluid feel intentionally heavy, because you're a big, burly, billionaire dressed as a bat.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.700
A lot of bees in there.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.680
It's beautiful.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.440
So, yeah, I don't know.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:33.780
I think the jury's still loud on feeling like Batman, but yeah, I feel at least like a unique character.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:43.820
See, I will say that taking out all the context of today, and taking out the idea of Arkham Asylum games,

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:51.940
in 1990, I'd say that this loosely makes me feel like Batman, in much more subtle ways.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:57.520
But I think that that heaviness, or weight to the character that you're talking about, Sean, really stood out to me.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:03.660
And I think that usually when we talk about weight to a character, we are talking about Mario as the gold standard,

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.340
because he has that momentum, and he slides a bit.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.780
But this is more the opposite.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:15.420
You feel heavy in the fact that you stick in where you are, where you feel like you're like Batman,

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:16.760
and you're throwing your weight around.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.720
And I'm not the biggest Batman guy, so maybe this isn't the way that he fights,

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:24.020
but when I picture Batman, he's not Spider-Man.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.260
He's not doing acrobatics, he's not jumping around.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:29.960
He's planting himself and punching people hard.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.440
And I did feel like I was doing that.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:37.980
Yeah. But he still has some acrobatics, but it's in a much more...

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.120
physical way.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:44.720
Yeah, it's a lot more precision, and they feel like the way Batman would do acrobatics.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:51.700
Yeah. And this may not be totally in line with what we were just saying,

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:56.060
but there's also this kind of Prince of Persia feel to it,

00:09:56.140 --> 00:10:01.440
with how central to navigation wall jumping is.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:07.020
And as far as NES games go, this is sort of the gold standard, I feel, to wall jumping.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:20.340
Again, it feels heavy, but it also has an ease to it that still feels skill-based,

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:28.420
that I think just shows you whether it's light or heavy or whatever adjective you want to use.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.640
It is well designed.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:34.480
The wall jump here is a little different than what we saw in Ninja Gaiden,

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.920
where Ryu would just kind of hang on the wall.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:45.420
But it's also different from other wall jumps where it requires incredibly precise timing on your wall jump.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:52.880
This feels, at the same time, it feels as good as Ryu's, but with a little more...

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.520
You know, you still have to...

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:55.720
You can't just hang on the wall.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:00.120
You do have to press the A button off the wall to go to jump to the other direction.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.060
But kind of like how you press the A button, too...

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:08.120
Yeah. Both on a wall jump and in just a regular jump, like, affects it as well,

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.580
which is like a nice touch to all the platforming.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:15.020
In the manual, it describes it as a normal jump, which is just tapping the A button,

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.160
and then a press and hold, which is the Batman jump.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.940
And even though they don't really do it in the pixel art,

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:28.320
I got the impression that the Batman jump has, like, the maneuverability of using the cape.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:31.260
Yeah. Where it, like, holds a little bit, and I agree.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:39.120
I think that, in a weird way, some people will complain about the sluggishness of Batman,

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:41.760
but in the way that they've laid out the game here,

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:45.440
the way that, like, enemies don't just constantly spawn on screen,

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:50.720
the platforming is just as important as the action element,

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:55.600
so you kind of have to both deal with, you know, pitfalls, but also deal with enemies.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:03.140
Like, I feel like they got it right in terms of where Batman should be on the acrobatic side,

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.800
but also on the dealing with enemies.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:14.860
That said, there are totally moments in this game that the enemies aren't well placed.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:23.240
And there are times in this game where I've felt, like, you either use the, one of the Batman weapons,

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:27.220
which is fine, right? I mean, you could do the pacifist run and not use the gun, right?

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:28.660
Like, they're all the same ammo.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.640
Whether you use the gun, the batarang, or the dirk,

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:35.240
it doesn't matter because they're all coming from the same ammo source.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:41.680
When you use them, you kind of have to because there are some, like, platforms that have an enemy there,

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:45.280
and, like, you'll either have to jump onto the platform and take some form of damage

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.780
before you can start wailing on them, or you use the item.

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:51.100
And then there's other times where it's like, well, it doesn't really matter either way

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:55.060
because you're just going to have to take some form of damage.

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:57.720
And I couldn't confirm that or not, but even just watching, like,

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:02.780
there was one particular thing on stage two where I was watching a long play

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.780
after I couldn't figure out, like, how not to take damage.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:07.600
And then they just skipped it too.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.100
They were like, no, I'm just going to take damage as well.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:15.640
Yeah, just tank it. Right, and I was like, what happens if that was your last, like, you know, bar on your health meter?

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.060
I think, yeah, you just got to restart.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:22.840
But I will say that there are definitely parts in this game, particularly boss fights,

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:27.380
where having ammo for the boss fight is imperative.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:32.760
Like, I don't even think it's possible, especially with the boss of level 2,

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:38.580
which is just sort of like this Rube Goldberg machine of shit just getting shot at you.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.200
I don't think you can punch everything.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.900
I think you can, actually.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:50.900
Really? Because I got there the first time, yeah, this funny, like, boss, which is, like, the room is the boss.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.640
But I got there the first time without any ammo.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:59.060
And unfortunately, I was kind of dying already, but I got to a point where I would, like,

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:03.540
duck under the thing that's shooting at me, jump up, and punch between every shot.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:04.980
Because it would do, like, a...

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.580
It would, like, shoot three bullets and then, like, retract for a second.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.420
So I could, like, duck under the bullets, jump up, punch a couple times.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:15.140
I ended up dying anyways, but I was making progress.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.940
Then I went back there and beat it much more easily with weapons.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.640
Sounds incredibly tedious. Yeah.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.040
But it didn't seem, like, crazy.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:27.740
Like, it didn't seem like it was, like, going to take me a half hour if I could have not died.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:28.760
But who knows?

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:36.780
It does, though, you know, because you are limited in the ammo, it does create some awkward moments with the fist fighting where,

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:45.080
if you know an enemy is coming, you just kind of stand in place and just punch repeatedly until the enemy kind of, like, walks into you.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.080
I don't know if you guys did that specifically.

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:49.080
But, like, yeah, I don't know.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.760
That's not something Batman would do.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.600
It's something that works in this game.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:55.740
But it's an awkward thing instead of a...

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.620
And, look, this game doesn't have to be, like...

00:14:57.740 --> 00:15:01.780
Arkham Asylum where every takedown is cool and slow-mo and stuff like that.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.320
Like, I'm not asking for that.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.720
I do just wish that they figured out a way...

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:10.600
I don't know. Bat gadgets or bat weapons, whatever they're called.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:19.220
Like, those things are so a part of the character that I would have liked to have seen them just be more than just projectiles.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:23.840
Yeah, particularly... I mean, I don't mind some of them being projectiles.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:29.700
I know I kind of joked about it before, but, like, that boomerang, that should just be a thing that you have.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.280
Yeah. Like, contextually but also gameplay-wise, it would have been nice.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:38.240
I think it would have helped with balance, because I know that we've been touching upon it, but...

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:48.620
This is just a very hard game, and losing any kind of ranged attack is pretty crippling, unless you have devoted a significant amount of time to mastering this game.

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:58.000
So, having at least this sort of low-range batarang just always with you would have been helpful.

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:41.800
And it's one of those hard games, too, because I feel like Batman's, as they described in the manual, power life.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:51.740
