00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:43.320
But there isn't, like, a respawn button, so...

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.280
I don't know.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.100
That was just sort of my experience with it.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:57.000
I found myself more managing my deaths, if that makes any sense, where I would just try to get to the boss with one life left.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:05.120
Because then I knew that I could die and restart and still be at the boss without getting a game over, where I'd have to go back to the beginning of the stage.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:13.680
But I'd die with one life left, still be at the boss, and then I could kill the boss with my gadgets, hopefully.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:17.060
Then I would go on to the next stage, just die on purpose.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:28.780
So that way I start the next stage right away with, like, all three or four of my lives, and try to get to the next boss with at least one life left, so I can respawn, you know, and just kind of kept doing it that way.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:34.180
